# Allowlist, not a denylist.
#
# This repo is versioned directly at ~/.config, where applications create new
# state directories on their own schedule. Under a denylist every one of them
# is untracked-but-committable until someone remembers to exclude it — that is
# how a directory holding a live IAM token nearly got committed. Here anything
# new is ignored by default and has to be named to be tracked.

*

# Repo metadata and tooling
!.github/
!.github/**
!.gitignore
!.gitleaks.toml
!.gitmodules
!.pre-commit-config.yaml
!.prettierignore
# Shared baseline for detect-secrets — belongs in the repo
!.secrets.baseline
!CLAUDE.md
!README.md
!bootstrap.sh
!doctor.sh

# Tracked tool configs. Both the directory and its contents need re-including:
# git does not descend into an excluded directory, so `!nvim/**` alone is inert.
!alacritty/
!alacritty/**
!nvim/
!nvim/**
# Named file by file: OpenCode reads opencode.json and auth.json from this
# directory, and those hold internal hostnames and credentials.
!opencode/
!opencode/AGENTS.md
!opencode/README.md
!opencode/commands/
!opencode/commands/mr-review.md
!opencode/commands/test.md
!opencode/instructions/
!opencode/instructions/python-conventions.md
!opencode/instructions/security-rules.md
!tmux/
!tmux/**
!zsh/
!zsh/**

# Machine-local overrides — keys, work-specific PATH and aliases. Never tracked.
zsh/*.local

# Claude Code drops per-directory state inside the trees above
.claude/

# zsh runtime artifacts
zsh/.zcompdump*
zsh/.zsh_history
zsh/.zsh_sessions/
